      "round": 1,
      "round_summary": "Round 1: Fix for `restart_output_correct`. Error type: DUT bug. Root cause: in state sB (line 80), `DATA_OUT := 0.U` unconditionally cleared the output register. When `io.RESTART` was already asserted during sB, on the first sC cycle `DATA_OUT` was 0 instead of `avg(RMAX,RMIN)`. Fixed by conditionally computing `DATA_OUT` in sB: `DATA_OUT := Mux(io.RESTART, avg(io.DATA_IN, io.DATA_IN), 0.U)`. When RESTART is high during sB, DATA_OUT is pre-loaded with `avg(DATA_IN, DATA_IN)` which equals `avg(RMAX,RMIN)` since both RMAX and RMIN are set to DATA_IN in sB. Only one line changed. Assertion label `restart_output_correct` preserved unchanged.",
