      "round": 2,
      "round_summary": "Round 2: Fix four assertion_error properties (pipeline_reg1_to_reg2, pipeline_reg2_to_reg3, pipeline_reg3_to_reg4, rlast_update_on_enable). Root cause: all four assertions compared an updated register against its source without accounting for Chisel's parallel-update semantics. On the next-cycle check, REG1 has already been updated with io.DATA_IN while REG2 holds old REG1 — so REG2 !== REG1. Same structural bug exists in all three pipeline assertions (REG3 vs REG2, REG4 vs REG3) and in rlast_update_on_enable (RLAST vs io.DATA_IN, where io.DATA_IN may change). Fix: use RegNext to snapshot the antecedent-cycle combinational value explicitly — REG2 === RegNext(REG1), REG3 === RegNext(REG2), REG4 === RegNext(REG3), RLAST === RegNext(io.DATA_IN). All four assertion labels preserved exactly. Homologous repair: pipeline_reg1_to_reg2, pipeline_reg2_to_reg3, pipeline_reg3_to_reg4 are structurally identical shifted-register comparisons, all repaired with the same RegNext pattern.",
