      "round_summary": "Round 3: Fix two remaining failing assertions. (1) `restart_output_correct`: changed from `fvAssert(!(sC && RESTART) || DATA_OUT===avg(...))` to `assertNextStepWhen(sC && RESTART, DATA_OUT===avg(...))`. Root cause: DATA_OUT is a register updated on the next cycle, but fvAssert checked same-cycle values. (2) `rlast_update_on_enable`: replaced `RegNext(io.DATA_IN)` inside `assertNextStepWhen` with an explicit snapshot register `rlast_snapshot` that captures `io.DATA_IN` when the condition is true. Root cause: `RegNext` inside `assertNextStepWhen` created a double-delay (one from assertNextStepWhen advancing to next cycle, another from RegNext), causing mismatches when ENABLE is not asserted every cycle. Both assertion labels preserved exactly. No homologous assertions found for restart_output_correct (unique structural pattern). For rlast_update_on_enable, no other structurally identical assertions in the source.",
